    "created_at": "2024-03-26T05:42:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-26T05:42:56Z",
    "body": "I am not speaking for any particular implementation team, but I suspect that implementations will not want to deal with the compat fallout of changing UA styles here.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, I don't think we should change HTML's conformance criteria around `<li>` elements. If you use them outside an `<ol>` or `<ul>`, your HTML validator should give you an error.\r\n\r\nSo the most practical route here seems to me to be changing the AT mapping to match the visual mapping, so that invalid list items are displayed to AT users the same way they are to sighted users.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
